From e4d861a0a115cf5852441737994e25cb4897d068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 13:21:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00668/11362] [outer-loop] Sudoku AR baseline: headroom
 CONFIRMED (the control P1 lacked)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AR transformer (3.2M params, matched compute, 15k steps, Sudoku-Extreme):
blank-cell-acc 0.342 (3x the 0.11 chance — AR IS learning) but exact-grid
solve-rate 0.002 greedy / 0.000 SC@32, mean 7.6 constraint violations. This is
the NON-DEGENERATE weak-AR regime: AR learns local patterns but cannot enforce
global constraints — real headroom (<<0.75), and crucially NOT the undertrained
collapse that made P1 inconclusive. The comparison is now meaningful.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
